formative"}], "description": "Why it matters: Documentary theory distinguishes forms of truth claim, voice, observation, and performance."}, {"id": "51ff88b7-0ca2-416b-bb23-dd68d3e49b54", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Evidence and ethics", "children": [{"id": "fd16cc59-5ec5-4287-8675-a2b28bc33e8e", "type": "concept", "title": "Consent"}, {"id": "dfc6d631-f3de-4abb-9262-a7339d5bb864", "type": "concept", "title": "Voice"}, {"id": "578d1de3-c70a-4a54-a457-5cf3ee7d4904", "type": "concept", "title": "Witnessing"}, {"id": "ff954d0c-3998-4ca3-8091-83a9c8741b01", "type": "concept", "title": "Staged reality"}], "description": "Why it matters: Nonfiction images carry responsibilities around consent, context, harm, and truth."}, {"id": "9a25c520-1f68-4ef7-af11-56e9ab1b5a74", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Essay and experimental nonfiction", "children": [{"id": "f4263c42-ed36-4a5e-8f44-bbb1c030f960", "type": "concept", "title": "Essay film"}, {"id": "bdfafe3e-124b-40ed-8c25-bdcda925a0b1", "type": "concept", "title": "Archive film"}, {"id": "422762e3-56a4-4de7-9ec7-86584c50a7f8", "type": "concept", "title": "Ethnographic film"}, {"id": "6ed940f6-d836-4d4b-b9f8-ff1d622fc601", "type": "concept", "title": "Reflexivity"}], "description": "Why it matters: Nonfiction can also be reflexive, poetic, archival, or essayistic."}]}, {"id": "f2650804-5274-4d05-b592-558a10e5ca9e", "type": "topic", "title": "Cognitive, Phenomenological, Affect, and Post-Theory Approaches", "description": "Introduce theories of perception, embodiment, emotion, cognition, and debates over grand theory.", "children": [{"id": "596e2930-aae7-456c-8050-05e0bd0e8ccc", "type": "subtopic", "title": "Cognitive film theory", "children": [{"id": "2af11a3b-8f69-4914-bccb-b7a2acd6f157", "type": "concept", "title": "Narrative comprehension"}, {"id": "3de40a43-1fa9-42b0-a8a1-36bc53fbbb9f", "type": "concept", "title": "Schema"}, {"id": "152bca76-fe93-4ca0-add6-d5509847791d", "type": "concept", "title": "Emotion"}, {"id": "d4cd0